From cbd9aa0f4dfa595a1eb6f46f31ddaf88b6e028a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Vanderberg <jvanderberg@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:35:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Add a riscv32 target (rv32ima, ilp32, soft float)

riscv32-gen.c is a code generator for rv32ima with the ilp32 ABI: long
long in register pairs, float and double in integer registers with the
libgcc soft-float helpers, long double as the ABI's 128-bit quad in
memory (computed in double precision). No compressed instructions are
emitted. The linker and assembler share the riscv64 files; RISC-V on
32 bits uses RELA relocations. lib/atomic-rv32.S and atomic-rv32-8.c
replace atomic.S, whose riscv code is rv64c.
